## Serial_Communication_Basics.md (new Fundamentals document)

Since frame structure (8N1, 7E1, etc.) is a fundamental concept that applies across UART, RS-485, Modbus, and other serial protocols, it gets its own document in `Fundamentals/`.

### Topics covered

| Topic | Description |
|---|---|
| Data bits | 7-bit vs 8-bit vs 9-bit, when to use each |
| Parity | None, Even, Odd — how parity bits are calculated |
| Stop bits | 1 vs 1.5 vs 2, effect on baud rate efficiency |
| Common configs | 8N1, 8E1, 7E1, 9N1 — comparison table |
| Start bit | Why always LOW, how receiver synchronises |
| Baud rate | Calculation, common values, clock error tolerance |
| Frame diagram | ASCII waveform showing start → data → parity → stop |
| Oversampling | 8× vs 16× sampling, noise rejection |

This document will be **referenced from** `Protocols/UART.md`, `Protocols/Modbus.md`, `Protocols/RS485.md`, etc. — avoiding duplication.

